  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Monday)\nIssued at 1248 PM CDT TUE SEP 1 2026\n\nThe center of the stout upper-level ridge remains situated over\nTennessee and Kentucky, where it will remain for much of the\nremaining workweek. While this ridge will keep things suppressed\nat the surface through Wednesday, there are at least low\nprobabilities for an isolated shower or storm today and tomorrow.\nOtherwise, dry conditions are expected to prevail for most of the\nregion. By Thursday, the ridge will slightly reorient itself,\nallowing for a weak disturbance to move toward the NW from the\nGulf. Rain chances will increase into Thursday, with the best\nrain chances along and south of I-85.\n\nThe main weather story into the weekend will remain the increased\nheat risk, with a Heat Advisory now in effect until 8 PM\nSaturday. Confidence is high that heat index values will range\nbetween 105 and 107 degrees into the weekend, with an increased\nrisk for people on concrete or asphalt for extended periods of\ntime. This will be especially important this weekend, given the\namount of outdoor events we expect to take place for the start of\ncollege football season. Low shower and thunderstorm\nprobabilities (20-30%) will also return this weekend, as the\nupper-level ridge reorients itself once again. With that being\nsaid, confidence in exact storm locations is low, as this\nactivity is generally expected to be scattered in nature.\n\n/44/",
